"""The sign-in with OpenID Connect providers (ADR 0020).

The flow is the authorization code flow with PKCE. `GET
/auth/providers/<name>/start` sends the browser to the provider. The
provider sends the browser back to `GET /auth/providers/<name>/callback`
with a code. The app changes the code for an ID token at the provider,
checks the token, and gives its own bearer token, as the sign-in with a
password does. A signed cookie holds the state, the nonce, and the PKCE
verifier of the flow between the two requests.

With `return_to` (a page of a front end in `CORS_ORIGINS`), the callback
sends the browser back to the page with the token in the fragment of the
URL: `#access_token=...&token_type=bearer&expires_in=...`, or `#error=...`.
Without `return_to`, the callback returns the token as JSON.
{% if grouped %}

A provider with `roles` sets the role of the user at each sign-in, from
the groups in a claim of the ID token.
{% endif %}
{% if signs_out %}

`GET /auth/providers/<name>/sign-out?return_to=...` sends the browser to
the logout URL of a provider with `sign_out`: the provider ends its
session, and sends the browser back to `return_to`. The front end deletes
the token of the app first.
{% endif %}
"""

